    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate field reconstruction",
    "problem": "Existing sea level pressure reconstructions for the pre-1850 period lack crucial marine data, poorly representing oceanic atmospheric circulation and limiting the ability to accurately study past climate changes in Europe without the risk of circular reasoning with other climate reconstructions.",
    "method": "The authors propose a new seasonal sea level pressure (SLP) dataset statistically reconstructed back to 1750 by combining terrestrial instrumental pressure series with marine wind information from ship logbooks using a multivariate principal component regression method.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct seasonal sea level pressure fields for the North Atlantic, Europe, and Mediterranean back to 1750 using instrumental pressure series and marine wind information from historical ship logbooks.",
