    "innovation": "This paper presents a new gridded seasonal sea level pressure reconstruction for the North Atlantic and Europe back to 1750, created by combining terrestrial pressure series with marine wind information from ship logbooks to improve reconstructions of past atmospheric circulation, particularly over the ocean.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "North Atlantic Oscillation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Europe",
            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "These atmospheric processes are connected with quasi-stationary patterns of climate variability such as the North Atlantic Oscillation (NAO) related to typical temperature and precipitation patterns in Europe (e.g. Hurrell 1995; Hurrell and van Loon 1997; Wanner et al. 2001).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "prolonged winter drought",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Mediterranean region",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "More recently, the prolonged winter drought in the Mediterranean region since the early 1960s has been attributed to different circulation states and can only partly be explained by single teleconnection patterns (e.g. D\u00fcnkeloh and Jacobeit 2003; Xoplaki et al. 2004; Paredes et al. 2006).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "HadSLP2",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "SLP",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "As predictand the seasonally averaged, 5\u00b0 \u00d7 5\u00b0 gridded instrumental SLP dataset HadSLP2 by Allan and Ansell (2006) was used, covering the period 1850\u20132004.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "European cooling",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Europe",
            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "On the southern flank of this continental anticyclone, cold air advection led to a widespread European cooling (Luterbacher et al. 2007).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "warmest European winters",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Europe",
            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "Indeed the winter of 1843 was among the warmest European winters in the period 1500-1900 (Luterbacher et al. 2004, 2007).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "coldest winter",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Midwest and Northeast US",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Interestingly, this winter was one of the coldest in the Midwest and Northeast US with a strong and persistent blocking situation (Ludlum 1968; Rosendal 1970).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Azores High",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "eastern North Atlantic",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "A key objective of this study is to improve the reconstruction skill over the eastern North Atlantic, thereby providing more reliable representations of the Azores High and the Icelandic Low.",
